      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit, why did you add \"maybe\" here? \"getOrCreate\" is a pretty common naming pattern -- compare https://source.corp.google.com/search?q\u003d%5CbgetOrMaybeCreate%20package:%5Eandroid%20case:no to https://source.corp.google.com/search?q\u003d%5CbgetOrCreate%20package:%5Eandroid%20case:no\u0026sq\u003d.\n\n\"getOrMaybeCreate\" sounds to me like there are 3 possible outcomes -- \"if it\u0027s available return it. Otherwise, create a new instance _when certain conditions are met_. Otherwise return null\".\n\nIf you\u0027re talking about \"get or create or throw\", then the \"throw\" is really a situation that shouldn\u0027t happen, so I wouldn\u0027t reflect to its name. Otherwise, if you only look at the callsite -- e.g. `Loader ld \u003d getOrMaybeCreate()` -- to me, I\u0027d look like `ld` may be null. (but it won\u0027t.)",
